{"id": "EUVD-2026-76495", "enisaUuid": "b744263f-a37b-3706-8416-a7193277388d", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nBluetooth: eir: Fix OOB read in eir_get_service_data()\n\neir_get_service_data() walks the advertising data for a Service Data\nfield with a matching UUID.  On a mismatch it advances:\n\n    eir += dlen;\n    eir_len -= dlen;\n\neir_get_data() reports dlen as the field's data length, but the field\nspans dlen + 2 bytes once its length and type bytes count, and more\nwhen non-Service-Data fields were skipped to reach it.  The pointer\nlands correctly on the next field.  eir_len does not, and the shortfall\ncompounds across fields until eir_get_data() reads the length and type\nbytes of a \"field\" past the end of the buffer.\n\nFor an ISO broadcast sink that buffer is hcon->le_per_adv_data[], filled\nfrom the periodic advertising reports of a remote broadcaster.  A PA\npayload packed with mismatching Service Data fields walks off the array\ninto the rest of struct hci_conn.  A drifted field that matches the BAA\nUUID puts those bytes in iso_pi(sk)->base, where user space reads them\nback with getsockopt(BT_ISO_BASE).\n\nRecompute eir_len from the end of the buffer each iteration.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:44:49", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:49:16", "baseScore": 8.1, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b6902adf81ea2ce14b1040dd97b6980050a8125a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1a28aae7f1fc8c06c0d02f153541be4fc7bacb74", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/815fc98c227a78cbd93d4c29f2833705b7c2bc0f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c21fa79301d7d6ac0a4ec6c51e8ba10beaa08c50", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bb56e97bd67614238c1c0a4084704ccadbb875b4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4beb198bc59b242404a47c21990bc84165052c8a"], "aliases": ["GHSA-q3pj-rcr4-5rqx", "CVE-2026-89583"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.27, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "07ff0c0e-d45e-3895-8d96-8761232c84ca", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8f9ae5b3ae80f168a6224529e3787f4fb27f299a <b6902adf81ea2ce14b1040dd97b6980050a8125a"}, {"id": "272620d9-c8a8-3aec-aa66-f73c478beb4d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8f9ae5b3ae80f168a6224529e3787f4fb27f299a <1a28aae7f1fc8c06c0d02f153541be4fc7bacb74"}, {"id": "33986bfb-5723-3bb1-b880-087d82ae95fc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8f9ae5b3ae80f168a6224529e3787f4fb27f299a <c21fa79301d7d6ac0a4ec6c51e8ba10beaa08c50"}, {"id": "39498b3e-a23d-312d-81cc-a8d9ce5ebf0e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.188"}, {"id": "59d80c15-8282-3b40-9cf3-ea70658775f8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8f9ae5b3ae80f168a6224529e3787f4fb27f299a <4beb198bc59b242404a47c21990bc84165052c8a"}, {"id": "74b4bb3b-34af-318d-bcd6-6e8a73750e6a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}, {"id": "753fc651-2746-3a04-92d8-0de8437c47c0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.19"}, {"id": "7e3f7411-5ab4-3e29-a502-7b40c9f5ffc6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.109"}, {"id": "980d3c4c-4f07-3ac6-868f-f99df75b0bba", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "a503ea89-1ea5-3a66-985d-49396879f5c1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "a79d0f93-3836-3169-9ea3-d066a06603de", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8f9ae5b3ae80f168a6224529e3787f4fb27f299a <815fc98c227a78cbd93d4c29f2833705b7c2bc0f"}, {"id": "c37750a0-99f0-3c59-a4b7-251a069d92ef", "product": {"nam